WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.011
Second Normal Form becomes especially relevant when

00:00:03.037 --> 00:00:06.964
a table has a composite key Suppose

00:00:06.991 --> 00:00:09.293
the row is identified by appointment ID

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.256
and service code together Now ask whether

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:15.322
every non-key column depends on that whole

00:00:15.335 --> 00:00:20.066
combination Appointment start time depends only on

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:23.490
the appointment Service name and standard price

00:00:23.516 --> 00:00:26.766
depend only on the service code Quantity

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.621
and the captured charge may depend on

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:32.687
the combination of appointment and service The

00:00:32.714 --> 00:00:34.490
columns that depend on only part of

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:36.174
the composite key should be moved to

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:40.454
the table where that dependency belongs This

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.836
leads toward separate appointment service and
appointment-service

00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:47.452
tables The goal is to align each

00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:49.610
fact with the key that actually determines

00:00:49.623 --> 00:00:49.820
it
